ive and sumNegative: duplicate loops with a no-op else branch (`total + 0`). The codebase idiom is `.reduce`, for example controller/src/stages/standard/backup.ts:195 and facts.ts:473. Use `values.filter(v => v > 0).reduce((s, v) => s + v, 0)`, or one shared helper `sumWhere(values, pred)`. Cost: about 24 lines for two near-identical copies, and the sign rule is written twice.\n- [S3] prototype/clunky.ts:28-34 isEmpty: `if (x) return true else return false` around a boolean expression. `values.length === 0` is the body. Callers can write `values.length === 0` directly and no wrapper is needed. There is no shared `isEmpty` in controller/src or dashboard/src.\n- [S3] prototype/clunky.ts: nothing imports the file and nothing tests it (grep found no references). It is dead code unless it is meant as a fixture. Not a reuse issue, only a note.\n\nI found no existing shared numeric utility module in controller/src or dashboard/src to call instead. The only generic helper is `unique` in controller/src/stages/standard/lib.ts:199, which is O(n^2) and local to the standard stage. It is not worth importing across modules, so use `Set`.\n\n## Verdict: FIX"},"harnessNoteCount":1,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"62d3bf8911e3a270","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This agent's report was delivered to you as a message from \"ad34f281892e007d5\" (its SubagentHandback call). Read it there; it is not repeated here.\n"}],"resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","totalDurationMs":17368,"totalTokens":16940,"totalToolUseCount":5,"usage":{"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":506,"cache_read_input_tokens":15651,"output_tokens":781,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":506},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":781,"cache_read_input_tokens":15651,"cache_creation_